  "name": "Folic Acid",
  "code": "FOL",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ol><li><p>Normal Range: If the folic acid level falls within the established normal range, it indicates that the individual has sufficient folic acid levels in their body. This suggests no deficiency and is considered a positive result.</p></li><li><p>Low or Below Normal Range: A folic acid level below the normal range suggests a potential folic acid deficiency. Folic acid deficiency can occur due to inadequate dietary intake, malabsorption issues, certain medical conditions, or as a side effect of certain medications. Further evaluation and supplementation may be necessary to address the deficiency.</p></li><li><p>High or Above Normal Range: Elevated folic acid levels may be observed in cases of excessive supplementation or certain underlying conditions such as liver disease or leukemia. Additional testing and evaluation may be required to determine the cause of the elevated levels.</p></li></ol>",
